# How to verify this evidence bundle

Bundle: **{{ meta.title }}** · format `{{ meta.format }}` · records 0–{{ plan.max_seq }} of installation `{{ meta.installation }}`
Author label (self-declared): {{ meta.author_label }} · exported {{ meta.exported_local_time }} (local clock, unverified)

You do not need the original app, and you do not need to trust the author.

## Automatic

```bash
pip install "cryptography>=44" "rfc3161-client>=1.0.6"
python3 verify.py .            # or: python3 verify.py provenance-….zip
python3 verify.py . --json     # machine-readable
```

Exit code 0 means no record failed. Every record is reported as *pass*, *pass (Bitcoin anchor
pending)*, *warning* or *fail* with a failure code. The two kinds of time are reported
separately; author statements and claimed dates never count as verified times.

